  content: `Feedback: change-propagation discipline. For any change to a core data structure (requirements shape, project schema, document chain edge, new event_type, new project_type, new template field), apply the change-propagation checklist before declaring the change done. Why: surfaced by user feedback during the SA&D audit rev b - agency tooling has many consumers of any data structure (templates, parsers, slash commands, subagents, UI, scripts, CLAUDE.md sections, memory entries); without discipline, drift accumulates and slow-burning bugs appear. This is opportunity 17 from the SA&D audit and foundational to plan 0007. The canonical 7-step checklist (updated 2026-05-24): 0. Look up the structure in the master data-structure map (reference/data-structure-map.md) - find the section, read the current consumer list. 1. List every consumer - start from the map's list, add anything new it missed; if the structure isn't in the map yet, add it. 2. Update each consumer before declaring the change shipped. 3. Add a doc-QA check (project-hub's doc-qa.js) that validates propagation. 4. Regression test on at least one existing project. 5. Update memory with any new principle introduced. 6. Update CLAUDE.md in affected repos. 7. Update the data-structure map to reflect the new state. The canonical checklist template lives at D:\\Repos\\Command Center Plan\\reference\\change-propagation-checklist.md (created 2026-05-25 in plan 0007 R0.1). CLAUDE.md sections referencing this discipline are live in Command Center Plan, GlensToolkit, project-hub, and icu-tools as of 2026-05-25.`
