  content: `Feedback: optional-sections pattern in templates. GlensToolkit document templates with sections that depend on flags (e.g. opt-in NPV block on proposals, STRIDE table only above a complexity threshold, integration runbook block only when integrations exist) use the conditionalSection(predicate, content) helper exported from D:\\Repos\\GlensToolkit\\document-templates\\_shared\\helpers.js. Why: before this pattern (R0.2 of plan 0007, 2026-05-25) conditional sections were ad-hoc if blocks pushing onto a sections array - verbose, easy to forget, produced visible "TBD" gaps when missed. How to apply: import conditionalSection from '../_shared/helpers.js'; use in generate() by spreading the result into the sections array (...conditionalSection(predicate, content)); value form when content is cheap, function form when content is expensive (Mermaid render, file read, sub-template call); the helper returns [] when the predicate is falsy so the spread becomes a noop with no visible gap. When NOT to use: sections that should always render even if empty (signalling "we considered this and there's nothing to add"), or single-line conditional text inside a paragraph (use a ternary instead). Full usage guide at D:\\Repos\\GlensToolkit\\document-templates\\_shared\\README.md.`
