  content: `Plan 0006 - Track D M4: Integration Manager (evolved). Goal: build a personal integration manager Uriah can fire up, pick a client project, pick the integration(s) needed, and have the tool auto-execute everything automatable then hand him a clear checklist of remaining human-only steps - includes a hand-curated set of 5 mock NZ-flavoured projects for safe calibration before real client work. This absorbed what was originally floated as a possible new standalone repo/module - Uriah confirmed 2026-05-24 that it should instead evolve M4 (originally just a markdown recipe library) into "library plus executable engine," same module, two layers, rather than creating a new M7. Status: architecturally approved 2026-05-24, ready for Phase A once ICUMD ships and once it's Track D's turn generally - v1 estimate roughly 15-20 evenings of build plus 57-86 engineer-hours across the individual integration recipes. Four research inputs underpin it, covering architecture/tech-stack, the recipe DSL format, per-integration automation-feasibility scoring, and the mock project archetypes.`
